   "fix": "In all three docstrings, say `QuadraticAlgebra R 0 0` (or `R[X]/(X\u00b2)`) instead of 'the repeated-root algebra'.",
   "issue": "The module docstring says 'In the repeated-root algebra the norm of `x + y\u03c9` is `x\u00b2`, its trace is `2x`' right after the paragraph on the general `QuadraticAlgebra R a b` with `a = -r\u00b2`, `b = 2r`. In that algebra the norm is `(x + ry)\u00b2` and the trace is `2x + 2ry`, so this overclaims. The same wording appears in the docstrings of `norm_eq_re_mul_re` (~line 89) and `trace_eq_two_mul_re` (~line 93), whose statements are only about `QuadraticAlgebra R 0 0`.",
